cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this library, please cite it as below."
title: "formal-martingales: Ville's inequality and anytime-valid martingale tools in Lean 4"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 library, built on mathlib, formalizing Ville's inequality for
  nonnegative supermartingales in finite-horizon and anytime forms, with the
  probability-normalized corollaries used in sequential analysis. The library
  is the supermartingale and time-uniform companion to mathlib's Doob-side
  martingale infrastructure, aimed at e-values, e-processes, and confidence
  sequences.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sneiderman
    given-names: Rob
    email: robbysneiderman@gmail.com
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Robby955/formal-martingales"
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - mathlib
  - martingale
  - Ville's inequality
  - anytime-valid inference
  - sequential analysis
  - formal mathematics
references:
